## 2. User Roles & Permissions (RBAC)

FinSight enforces strict tenant isolation and Role-Based Access Control across multiple businesses[cite: 5, 6, 23]. One user account may belong to multiple businesses with distinct roles per business (e.g., an external accountant managing five SMEs)[cite: 6].

| Role | Description | Permitted Operations | Restricted Operations |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Business Owner (`OWNER`)** | Primary business principal[cite: 4]. | Full access to dashboard, revenue/expense analytics, invoicing, payments, reconciliation, reports, business settings, and team role management[cite: 4, 5, 6]. | Cannot access other tenants' data[cite: 23]. |
| **Accountant / Financial Admin (`ACCOUNTANT`)** | Internal or external financial practitioner[cite: 5]. | Review transactions, execute/confirm payment reconciliations, categorize expenses, generate/export financial reports, view audit histories[cite: 5, 16]. | Cannot delete the business entity or alter Owner ownership without explicit transfer. |
| **Employee / Staff (`STAFF`)** | Operational team member[cite: 5]. | Create/manage customers and draft/issue invoices (based on assigned scope)[cite: 5]. | Restricted from sensitive company-wide financial reports, cash-flow forecasts, audit logs, and business admin settings[cite: 5]. |

